<Project>

  <!-- Nothing from the repository's Directory.Build.props reaches the
       templates. A template is copied out of this tree by `dotnet new`
       and builds on a bare SDK, where none of the root's properties
       exist: no artifacts/ layout, no lock files, no CI build settings.
       The checkout has to see the same project the scaffold sees, so
       this file does not import the parent, unlike the one lane under
       hosts/ that keeps the root's settings and turns off only its lock
       files; this one stops the chain here.

       The visible symptom this prevents: an editor restoring the
       templates in place (the C# extension does, whenever a .csproj
       changes) wrote a packages.lock.json beside each one, because the
       root turns lock files on for every project. The file recorded
       only the part of the graph that resolved through the SHODDY-*
       placeholders, and git saw it as a new untracked file in a tree
       that should stay clean. With this file in the way, such a restore
       writes an obj/ folder, which is ignored, and nothing else. -->

</Project>
